Carafe: the profiler counts each sampled thread's time by the calls nearest the start of the game's own code, so the
stages of a game's frame loop show without knowing the game. While the thread is paused the sampler only copies the
x86 frame chain from the guest's EBP to the thread's start, up to 64 frames; a chain that breaks before it is left
out. Which frames belong to the game's .exe is asked only after the thread runs again and the profiler's own lock is
free, because the answer takes Wine's virtual_mutex, which the paused thread may hold; the answers are cached. From
the start it skips the system's frames to the first one inside the .exe, and the return addresses one to eight calls
from there each count the sample; every report adds a stages line with the three busiest at each level, as shares of
the samples that reached the game's code.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

